Possession of The Amulet will double the spell
power necessary to cast the spells; don't rely
on your Valkyrie's power. Instead use those
plenty of scrolls of teleport accmulated thus
far - I hope you did so.

> Potions
> of gain energy haven't been particularly in
> abundance this game, so unless somebody
> knows a nice easy recipe for those...  there
> are going to be times when I need to walk.

I'd use those potions for full healing alchemy.

> So I'm trying to make some nice easy paths
> through the mazes.
> 
> My question is, how much is clearly enough?

Usually, in my games, that depend on whether I
decide to ascend with pets or not. I so I dig
a couple squares around the stairs to quickly
magic whistle my pets around me. On teleport
levels I dig a direct connection between the
upstairs and downstairs (if the stairs are not
far away from each other), otherwise I rely on
my teleport scrolls. While exploring a level
in Gehennom, starting from the stairs (up or
down, depending on whether you explore Gehennom
top-down or bottum-up) I often explore the maze
close to the stairs first, and if there are too
twisted ways I dig through a wall for a short-
cut. On non-teleport levels I always try to
dig some short-cuts since teleport scrolls are
useless here. Also mind that the force may
place your character in some yet unexplored
territory; digging some diagonal path north
and south will make it easy to find good paths
later, and that will also disclose trapdoors
on that path; later those traps may be much
more inconvenient since you'll give the force
more opportunities to drag you back. The rest
that you may need do dig on your home-run can
be dug with one of the usually many available
wands of digging that you've likely collected.

That all said, let me tell you that I am not
too consequent to literally do that on every
level; it depends on the layout and my options.

> I've heard tell of people digging away *all* the
> walls in Gehennom, so that every level is a
> pure wide open field, but I'm pretty sure that's
